Package: miniLNM
Title: Miniature Logistic-Normal Multinomial Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Kris", "Sankaran", , "ksankaran@wisc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9415-1971"))
Description: Logistic-normal Multinomial models are common in problems with multivariate count data. This package implements a logistic-normal multinomial model using a 30 line Stan script. This lightweight implementation makes it an easy starting point for other projects. The logistic-normal multinomial model is often used to model "compositional" data -- it can be used whenever a multinomial probability parameter is thought to depend linearly on inputs in a transformed, log ratio space. For more details, please refer to the reference.
